  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q31-34-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Determine whether the following specifications of a triangle $\\triangle ABC$ can be drawn.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q31-34-part-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\angle A=30^\\circ$, $a=13\\text{ cm}$, $b=14\\text{ cm}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Possible.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin B}{14}&=\\frac{\\sin30^\\circ}{13}\\\\\\sin B&=\\frac{14\\sin30^\\circ}{13}\\\\\\sin B&=\\frac{7}{13}\\\\B_1&=\\sin^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{7}{13}\\right)\\approx32.58^\\circ\\\\B_2&=180^\\circ-B_1\\approx147.42^\\circ\\\\A+B_2&\\approx177.42^\\circ<180^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nBoth candidate angles give a positive third angle. A triangle is possible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q31-34-part-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\angle A=55^\\circ$, $a=7\\text{ cm}$, $b=20\\text{ cm}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not possible.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin B}{20}&=\\frac{\\sin55^\\circ}{7}\\\\\\sin B&=\\frac{20\\sin55^\\circ}{7}\\\\\\sin B&\\approx2.34043>1\\end{align*}$$\nNo angle has this sine value, so no triangle is possible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q31-34-part-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\angle A=40^\\circ$, $a=6.4\\text{ cm}$, $b=10.1\\text{ cm}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Not possible.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin B}{10.1}&=\\frac{\\sin40^\\circ}{6.4}\\\\\\sin B&=\\frac{10.1\\sin40^\\circ}{6.4}\\\\\\sin B&\\approx1.01440>1\\end{align*}$$\nThe unrounded sine value exceeds one, so no triangle is possible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q31-34-part-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\angle A=45^\\circ$, $a=8\\text{ cm}$, $b=11.2\\text{ cm}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Possible.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin B}{11.2}&=\\frac{\\sin45^\\circ}{8}\\\\\\sin B&=\\frac{11.2\\sin45^\\circ}{8}\\\\\\sin B&=\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{10}\\\\B_1&=\\sin^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{10}\\right)\\approx81.87^\\circ\\\\B_2&=180^\\circ-B_1\\approx98.13^\\circ\\\\A+B_2&\\approx143.13^\\circ<180^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nBoth candidate angles give a positive third angle. A triangle is possible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
